\1\n    <div id="site-header"></div>
    <!-- Header -->
    
    <main class="lesson-container py-4">
        <!-- Breadcrumb -->
        <div id="tutorial-header"></div>
        
        <div class="content lesson-content" style="font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--text-secondary);">
            <p>DHCP (Dynamic Host Configuration Protocol) automatically assigns IP addresses and network settings (like Subnet Mask and Default Gateway) to devices on a network.</p><h3>How It Works (DORA)</h3><ul><li><strong>Discover:</strong> Client broadcasts looking for a server.</li><li><strong>Offer:</strong> Server offers an IP.</li><li><strong>Request:</strong> Client requests the offered IP.</li><li><strong>Acknowledge:</strong> Server confirms the lease.</li></ul><h3>Troubleshooting Tip</h3><p>If your IP address starts with <code>169.254.x.x</code> (APIPA), your device failed to reach the DHCP server.</p>
        </div>
        
